  "articleBody": "Remodeling a mobile home can be exciting, but there are a few common missteps folks make that can turn a dream project into a headache. Let's chat about how to steer clear of them. First off, a big mistake is diving in without a full inspection. You might think you know what you're getting into, but hidden damage or structural issues can pop up unexpectedly. Always get a professional assessment first to uncover any surprises. Another common pitfall is underestimating hidden damage. Mobile homes can have unique quirks, and what looks like a small problem on the surface might be a sign of something bigger underneath. A thorough inspection helps here too! Then there's choosing materials or changes that just don't fit the home's construction limits. Mobile homes have specific structural considerations, so you can't always treat them like a stick-built house. Make sure your plans are realistic for the type of home you have. Lastly, sometimes folks forget to check if the home is HUD-code manufactured housing or clarify the title/ownership status before starting major work. This is super important and can save you headaches down the line. If you're planning a mobile home remodel, give us a call! We can help you avoid these mistakes and ensure your project goes smoothly.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
